ackingStore :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module FrontCache :: init: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module FrontCache :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module FrontCache :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- refinement obligation: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n\nLast bundle slug: write_through_cache\nParent module: WriteThroughCacheSystem\nModules: BackingStore(abs), BackingStore(impl), FrontCache(abs), FrontCache(impl)\nRevise the failing module(s) and/or abstraction map(s). Return one call to repair_module_bundle with the FULL revised bundle."}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-7', 'system': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are repairing a multi-module ModuleBundle that failed one or more proof\nobligations under TLC. The user message lists each failing obligation: it\nmay be a per-impl (Init/Consec/Property) failure, or the cross-module\nrefinement obligation.\n\nYour task\n---------\nDiagnose the failures and emit a revised bundle via the\n`repair_module_bundle` tool. Set `targeted_failure` to point at the most\nimportant failure (e.g. `"Queue/consec"`, `"refinement"`, `"parent/property"`).\nProvide 